  "notes": "\"Sugar trap\" turned punk-rap and nu-metal — glossy top-end against deliberately abrasive beats. The distinguishing parameter is the **808 treated as a riff instrument**: repeated 8th- and 16th-note root pulses rather than one long sustain, which nothing else in this lane does. Guitar-like distorted synth riffs carry the melody, and the kick-and-clap bus is clipped on purpose. ⚠ `medium`: the genre palette, per-track producers, chart status and her own statement about vocal treatment are documented; the research rates it high-medium.",
